itures, product development, and other liquidity requirements associated with our operations, with net cash provided by operating activities and borrowings under our credit facilities. From time to time, we have also issued debt to supplement our cash needs, repay our other indebtedness, or finance our acquisitions. We continue to expect that cash generated from our operating activities, together with borrowings under our revolving credit facility and other borrowing capacity, will be sufficient to fund our continuing operating needs for the next 12 months and the foreseeable future.","context":"LIQUIDITY AND CAPITAL RESOURCES","section":"RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":515,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-325790","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0000108312","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/108312/000119312526325790/wwd-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/e9d40c70de0430de615fd05302c5f825df5d9575c33fc50f5f36864835030794.bin","sha256":"e9d40c70de0430de615fd05302c5f825df5d9575c33fc50f5f36864835030794"}}],"omittedEvidenceCount":0},"managementExplanations":{"status":"evidence_available","evidence":[{"id":"e464cecafeba5f9069b5add8e69722644db6d675bea0cd5a90f02be0f83b6814","quote":"In May 2020, Woodward entered into five U.S. dollar intercompany loans payable, with identical terms and notional values of each tranche of the 2020 Fixed-Rate Cross-Currency Swaps, together with reciprocal fixed-rate intercompany cross-currency interest rate swaps. The agreements were entered into by Woodward Barbados Euro Financing SRL (\"Euro Barbados\"), a wholly owned subsidiary of Woodward, and are designated as cash flow hedges under the criteria prescribed in ASC 815. The objective of these derivative instruments is to hedge the risk of variability in cash flows attributable to the foreign currency exchange risk for future principal and interest payments associated with the U.S. dollar denominated intercompany loans over a 13 year period, as Euro Barbados maintains a Euro functional currency. For each of the fixed-rate intercompany cross-currency interest rate swaps, changes in the fair values of the derivative instruments are recognized in accumulated other comprehensive income (\"OCI\") and reclassified to foreign currency transaction gain or loss included in “Selling, general and administrative expenses” in Woodward’s Condensed Consolidated Statements of Earnings. Reclassifications out of accumulated OCI of the change in fair value occur each reporting period based upon changes in the spot rate remeasurement of the Euro and U.S. dollar denominated intercompany loans, including associated interest. Hedge effectiveness is assessed based on the fair value changes of the derivative instruments, and such hedges are deemed to be highly effective in offsetting exposure to variability in foreign exchange rates. There are no credit-risk-related contingent features associated with these fixed-rate cross-currency interest rate swaps.","context":"Derivative instruments in cash flow hedging relationships","section":"WOODWARD, INC.","block":173,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-325790","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0000108312","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/108312/000119312526325790/wwd-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/e9d40c70de0430de615fd05302c5f825df5d9575c33fc50f5f36864835030794.bin","sha256":"e9d40c70de0430de615fd05302c5f825df5d9575c33fc50f5f36864835030794"}},{"id":"051c1b513d7c622a43ce75ecd1811ceabede235b752bab903f93e999dd001fd1","quote":"The Company periodically reviews its business and from time to time may sell businesses, assets, or product lines as part of business rationalization. Any gain or loss recognized due to divestitures is recorded within the line item “Other income, net” in the Condensed Consolidated Statements of Earnings.","context":"Divestitures","section":"WOODWARD, INC.","block":202,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-325790","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0000108312","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/108312/000119312526325790/wwd-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/e9d40c70de0430de615fd05302c5f825df5d9575c33fc50f5f36864835030794.bin","sha256":"e9d40c70de0430de615fd05302c5f825df5d9575c33fc50f5f36864835030794"}},{"id":"9301230d6a6ef35eab70f7fd1e0a502f28fb974243ae46f2a1fdda3c5d2be512","quote":"The increases in the effective tax rates for the three months ended June 30, 2026 and the nine months ended June 30, 2026 compared to the same periods of the prior fiscal year were primarily attributable to the current year elimination of the U.S. intangible income tax benefit due to the one-time reversal of research costs previously capitalized, an increase in U.S. taxes on foreign earnings, a decrease in the tax benefit from stock-based compensation, a reduction to the U.S. Federal Research and Development Credit, and unfavorable state tax law changes.","context":"| | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | Three Months Ended June 30, | | | Nine Months Ended June 30, | | | 2026 | | | 2025 | | | 2026 | | | 2025 | Earnings before income taxes | | $ | 193,512 | | | $ | 126,836 | | | $ | 530,090 | | | $ | 361,653 | Income tax expense | | | 46,837 | | | | 18,388 | | | | 115,683 | | | | 57,165 | Effective tax rate | | | 24.2 | % | | | 14.5 | % | | | 21.8 | % | | | 15.8 | %","section":"WOODWARD, INC.","block":261,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-325790","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0000108312","url":"https://www.sec.